.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rev-stealth-vpn-rotate 1  "rev-stealth-vpn-rotate " 
.SH NAME
rev\-stealth\-vpn\-rotate \- Trigger a VPN rotation. With `lazy\-on\-fail`, rotation is skipped unless the failure counter has crossed the threshold
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrev\-stealth vpn rotate\fR [\fB\-\-provider\fR] [\fB\-\-strategy\fR] [\fB\-\-region\fR] [\fB\-\-reason\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-explain\fR] [\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Trigger a VPN exit\-IP rotation through the configured provider (Surfshark / Gluetun). Strategy `lazy\-on\-fail` skips when the failure counter is under threshold; `every\-n` / `interval` rotate unconditionally on cadence. The action is recorded to the audit log with the supplied \-\-reason.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-provider\fR \fI<PROVIDER>\fR [default: surfshark]
VPN provider slug (currently only `surfshark`)
.TP
\fB\-\-strategy\fR \fI<STRATEGY>\fR [default: lazy\-on\-fail]
Rotation strategy: `lazy\-on\-fail`, `every\-n`, `interval`
.TP
\fB\-\-region\fR \fI<REGION>\fR
Optional region (`jp`, `us\-west`, `de`, ...). Cycled through when omitted
.TP
\fB\-\-reason\fR \fI<REASON>\fR [default: manual]
Reason hint; recorded in the audit log for forensics
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5: side\-effect\-free plan emission. No file writes, no network calls, no keyring operations. Returns exit 0 after emitting the structured plan envelope
.TP
\fB\-\-explain\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5: include the action plan in the result envelope\*(Aqs `result.plan` field. Can be combined with `\-\-dry\-run`. When passed without `\-\-dry\-run`, the plan is emitted alongside the real action
.TP
\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR \fI<IDEMPOTENCY_KEY>\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5 / G.6: opaque caller\-supplied key for at\-most\-once commit semantics. Accepted in G.5; surfaced in the envelope; the underlying commit replay semantics land in G.6
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  $ rev\-stealth vpn rotate
  $ rev\-stealth vpn rotate \-\-strategy every\-n \-\-region jp \-\-reason scheduled
  $ rev\-stealth vpn rotate \-\-provider surfshark \-\-strategy interval \-\-reason failover

EXIT CODES:
  0  Ok               Rotation completed (or correctly skipped under lazy\-on\-fail).
  1  UserError        Unknown \-\-provider / \-\-strategy.
  2  TransientError   Provider/container transient failure.
  3  PermanentError   Provider unsupported in this build.
  7  Leak             Post\-rotation leak check failed (fail\-closed).

ENV:
  REV_SCRAPING_REQUIRE_VPN  When `1`, enforces VPN\-required guard policy\-wide.
